  "slug": "doubling-genome-bb89",
  "summary": "Pan-cancer and single-cell studies now date WGD against drivers and detect doubled subclones in tumours classed as non-WGD.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is the timing and detection of whole-genome doubling (WGD) in tumour evolution. A pan-cancer analysis of 41,332 tumours across 12 cancer types dates WGD relative to drivers, chromosomal losses and immune programmes. Single-cell analysis finds WGD subclones in tumours classed as non-WGD, and the expression-based WAGES method maps WGD clonal fraction in bulk tumours, indicating that clonal fraction and single-cell resolution extend beyond binary WGD status. Related work mapping mosaic chromosomal alterations across 19 tissues from 722 WGS samples, reporting recurrent mitotic error and purifying selection, concerns non-tumour tissue and is not doubling-specific. Remaining items address somatic variant calling, retrotransposition, sex-biased signatures and plant somatic mutation, and are peripheral to this thread.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-05"
}
